  "walk_audit": {
    "arrival_semantics": "native_gameplay.py:378-398: a 0x0087 walkok sets arrival only when its start position equals its destination (zero-cell walk), so a 1-cell walk confirms only via the NEXT walkok starting at the pending cell; if no rx frames flow at all the pending gate never opens.",
    "release_predicate": "playing_runtime.py:1219-1237 clears _pending only on `view.arrival_confirmed and pos.seq > seq and (pos.x, pos.y) == point`; otherwise it re-sends the SAME point after >=1.0s up to 3 retries, then raises NativeTelemetryUnavailable. A missing ack therefore holds wire sends silently instead of failing the dispatch.",
    "window2_attribution": "wire-send side: window 2's 16 dispatched MoveTo actions reached perform_native honestly (the dispatch counters sit upstream of every gate), but the pending-walk gate holds each dispatch while a walk is unacknowledged - playing_runtime.py:1061-1062 (`if self._await_pending(view, pos): return`) - so the only wire send was the first dispatch's single next-path-step at playing_runtime.py:1070-1073 (`point = path[1]; self.wire.move(*point)`), matching the observed 1-tile displacement.",
    "window3_discriminator": "frame_timeline rows pair dispatched_actions.moveTo with walk_sends (0x035F at the wrapped _send seam) and walk_acks (0x0087): sends present with zero acks = ack path blocker; zero actor frames = map-session ingestion blocker; attackable actors observed with acks flowing = travel/targeting blocker."
  }
